                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL:DR:\nThe game is purely about boss fights with dragons.  A little bit of story exists, but for the most part, fighting dragons is what this is about.  For a free to play game, the quality is fairly high. \n\nFirst Impression and Complete Gameplay: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=re7BAfIMb8Q&feature=youtu.be\n\nThe main character wields a sword which can do quick basic attacks and slow strong attacks.  You can chain attacks together to make combos.  It's a fairly simple system, but it works pretty well.\n\nYou also have the option of changing into your own dragon form, which appears to deal more damage and gives you the ability to life-steal with attacks.  This form is timed and works by charging a \"battery\" with your basic swords attacks in the other form.\n\nGraphics are pretty good for a free to play, and I have no complaints about it.  I enjoyed the different dragons designs, and each dragon requires a different strategy to defeat.\nAudio is pretty good as well.\n\nControls are responsive, but I dislike how dodge is defaulted to the shift key (sticky keys).  Luckily, you can rebind keys.\nAlso, if you click to attack as you dodge, your character will perform the attack immediately after the dodge animation completes.  This can lead to issues if you need to dodge again immediately to miss an enemy attack.\n\nPlaying through the entire game took me about 30 minutes, including failures and load times.  So the game is fairly short.  \nAll in all, this is a pretty fun game.  I'm impressed that it was made by a team who were still in college at the time.",
